Browser: guard sortPriority against an empty URL list

get-logins with a keepassxc://by-path/... or keepassxc://by-uuid/... lookup can
match an entry that has neither a URL nor additional URLs. sortEntries then
calls sortPriority with an empty list, priorityList stays empty, and
"return *std::max_element(priorityList.begin(), priorityList.end())"
dereferences end().

An empty URL list means no match, which is the priority 0 the function already
returns for a URL that matches nothing, so the guard keeps the semantics.

--- a/src/browser/BrowserService.cpp
+++ b/src/browser/BrowserService.cpp
@@ -1278,6 +1278,11 @@
 // extension provided site and form url.
 int BrowserService::sortPriority(const QStringList& urls, const QString& siteUrl, const QString& formUrl)
 {
+    if (urls.isEmpty())
+    {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     QList<int> priorityList;
     // NOTE: QUrl::matches is utterly broken in Qt < 5.11, so we work around that
     // by removing parts of the url that we don't match and direct matching others
